data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":1915,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"message","id":"msg_000c52aeac7fc640016b06b757146887d18f262c96dab99f30","role":"assistant","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"wren\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Develop a general hand-twist-fiber-cord operation with sample, make, inspect, trial and cancel modes. Related capabilities were searched: fiber returned hand-weave-fiber-mat and twist returned no match; broader cord/rope results were incomplete and do not establish absence. Within the available contracts, probe covers preliminary physical testing and hand-weave-fiber-mat covers plaited mats, not two-ply cord manufacture or cord load trials. Reuse their applicable implementation machinery rather than claim it as newly invented. The missing cord mechanism belongs in the current-conversation development handoff. Wren's verified plaiting result does not establish cord suitability or tensile strength.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"General interface: hand-twist-fiber-cord(mode, materials:[{stackId,quantity}], targetId, workId, requestedLength, trialForce, trialDuration). Modes are sample, make, inspect, trial and cancel; reject irrelevant arguments. Applicable to any learner with usable hands and reachable owned material, not only reeds or Wren. This is a development contract, not an executed action or inventory grant. Review and development waiting advance no simulation time. Record code dependencies and source references in the implementation: probe for observation/sample handling, hand-weave-fiber-mat for compatible fiber-lot provenance, reservations and condition handling, and existing world ownership, energy, work, event and rendering systems. Do not require learning mat weaving as a prerequisite.\\\\nStudy requires 3 actual study rounds at 0.2 energy each, paid individually; interrupted study retains paid progress. No tools, anchors, water, additional fibers or helpers are supplied. Work requires two usable hands, sufficient energy, reachable inputs and enough unoccupied space for the selected short cord; length is capped at 0.30 m in this initial manual version. Invalid submissions reserve and charge nothing. Input quantities use existing inventory precision, with a minimum sample of 0.1 unit and maximum manufacturing batch of 1 unit. Reserve exact selected stack quantities atomically, preserving source, processing, age, mass and condition. Do not select undisclosed inventory automatically.\\\\nSample: 1 round and 0.5 energy per 0.1-unit sample, attempting manual separation, bending, twisting and a small opposing-hand pull. The sample becomes a separately identified owned tested lot or damaged scrap, not vanished material. Report actual separation, retained twist, visible fractures and the bounded force applied, never a blanket suitability claim. Sample failure can preclude making from that tested lot, but applies only to represented matching material and condition. A prior mat test is evidence about plaiting only.\\\\nMake: requires a passing cord sample result covering the selected material's relevant source, processing and current condition; recheck deterioration and accessibility. Reserve inputs, then execute four paid rounds at 1 energy each: separate and align two bundles, twist the first section, counter-ply and extend, then release and check retained form. Each round moves only the recorded quantity actually handled into the workpiece. The first round determines feasible dimensions from available usable fiber and requested length; it may produce a measured shortfall instead of advancing. No invented splices, cutting tools or unlimited fiber extension. Failure during any step leaves the actual loose, twisted or damaged material rather than a complete cord. Completion requires two interlocked plies retaining a coherent form after release, with positive measured length and section. It grants no strength rating.\\\\nImplement the smallest physical mechanism needed in this handoff: represented usable fiber length/section, mass density, separability, bend response, twist retention, inter-ply slip and bounded tensile response. Reuse existing material properties where applicable, but mat flexibility and strength fields alone are not a calibrated cord tensile law. Derive dimensions from conserved material volume and actual fiber geometry, including twist shortening and overlap; do not assign dimensions merely because they were requested. Unknown stem length or moisture must not silently become favorable values. Where an essential property cannot be measured or supported by material definitions, execute only the supported physical sample/attempt, report the unresolved limitation and retain its real products; implement missing measurement/material support in this same handoff before enabling a claimed complete cord. No fixed-era unlock or unrelated activity roadmap.\\\\nInspect: owned reachable workpiece or cord, 1 round and 0.2 energy. Record measurable length, section range, ply count, loose ends, fraying, visible damage and current condition, with unknown fields explicit. Inspection does not determine untested breaking strength or repair damage. Trial: owned reachable cord, two usable hands, a span that can actually be gripped between those hands, force and duration explicitly selected. One trial occupies 1 round, costs 0.5 energy, and applies for at most that round's simulated duration; force is bounded by current hand capability and the cord's attainable grip, with requested and achieved force recorded separately. No body-weight, hanging, anchor or added-weight trial is supplied. Use a deterministic physical response to actual force, duration, section, material condition and grip; record slip, extension, retained deformation, fracture and unloaded condition. Stop at loss of grip or breakage. A pass means only survival of the achieved force for the measured duration, not general safety, safe working load or suitability for climbing. Broken cord becomes owned fragments with conserved total material and updated geometry. Trials cannot raise material strength by repetition.\\\\nEvery paid stage appends an immutable event with actor, work/item IDs, exact input/output lot IDs and quantities, elapsed time, energy, operation parameters, observations and outcome. Manufacture partitions inputs into material still reserved, incorporated material, returned offcuts and damaged scrap; all quantities and mass must balance, including any loss represented as recoverable debris at the site. Nothing duplicates or restores consumed effort. Outputs inherit relevant origin, age and processing history; carrying mass includes work and finished products. For this applicant, item-73-wren-819 is a possible selected raw source, item-85-wren-976 and item-85-wren-977 are offcuts whose usable geometry must be checked, and item-78-wren-870 has condition-zero tested-scrap processing and cannot be treated as intact stock. These references authorize no automatic consumption.\\\\nWork continues only on actual worked rounds, revalidating hands, reach, ownership, reservation, space and energy before charging each stage. Leaving reach, insufficient energy, incapacity or an unworked round pauses without charging the next stage; retain exact paid stage and material state. Resume by workId after revalidation, with no repeated completed-stage cost. Cancel is instantaneous and energy-free: release unworked reservations once and leave incorporated material as an owned unfinished item with its real state; paid time, energy and damage are never refunded. Restarting cancelled work cannot restore loose fiber or repeat refunds; usable unfinished material may be explicitly supplied to a later attempt. Death stops work and releases reserved material at the death site under ordinary estate/ownership rules, leaving the workpiece and fragments physically present and returning nothing to a new inventory.\\\\nThere is no passive production or automatic strength gain. Ordinary ageing and supported environmental deterioration continue while paused. No invented wear rate: reuse compatible existing lot-condition rules and explicitly register any new cord-specific wear law. Inspect after damage or deterioration before relying on an old trial; previous trials retain their historical conditions, not perpetual certification. Repair, attachment and structural use are not effects of this version. Finished cord is a real portable material item, not an automatic shelter, comfort or protection bonus. All validation, conservation, continuation and trial rules execute in code without repeated model review.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":3,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"No experience benefit for requesting, naming, registering, studying, querying or gaining nominal mastery. Verified new personal observations from real sampling, manufacture or load trials, including informative failures, may qualify under the existing experience rules; key evidence by functional operation, material/condition and observed outcome so repeated inspections, synonymous capabilities and retry loops do not farm novelty. Familiar successful practice may sustain only modest existing-rule satisfaction when personally applicable and grounded in paid physical participation. Any pleasure/satisfaction integration must use the existing bounded caps, decay and cooldown and deduplicate the underlying event; if no compatible evaluator exists, award none pending that handoff rather than alter protected accounts. This operation grants no physical-comfort bonus, changes no nutrition, goals, permissions or reward budgets, and confers no mastery or consent.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Register reusable fiber-work and cord visual metadata with state, material color, actual length and section, ply count, twist direction, loose ends, fraying, condition, visible damage, fragment IDs and work progress. Anchor animation and geometry changes to committed physical events: hands separating/twisting, a genuinely retained cord, measured hand tension, slippage or breakage. Distinguish reserved loose fiber, unfinished work, failed attempts, complete untested cord and the historical outcome of a specific trial. Display only measured dimensions; unknown properties remain unknown. No success animation for submission, study, paused or failed work, and no universal strength badge after one bounded trial. Reuse existing fiber rendering and event infrastructure where applicable and record that reuse separately from the new cord geometry.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}}

